cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Paperivore: a CAD/CAE toolchain grown by validating against papers"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Windows CAD/CAE toolchain (build123d, gmsh, CalculiX, PyVista)
  that is built incrementally by reproducing published papers: each paper becomes
  a benchmark, every mismatch is traced to the solver, the reference model, or the
  paper itself, and the fix is kept as a regression case.
message: "If you use this benchmark set, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Tianjian
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tianjian/paperivore"
keywords:
  - CAD
  - CAE
  - finite element
  - validation
  - open science
  - CalculiX
  - build123d